The Blood Spiral Brotherhood was founded by [[the Betrayer]], who betrayed his best friend, [[Lord Casterwill]], and became mortal enemies with his family when he attempted to perform a dark ritual on the [[Spiral Mark]], summoning Void to reactivate the Mark and use it as a beacon to call back the [[Nullifiers]] to earth. He was defeated by Lord Casterwill's children however, leaving the Blood Spiral Brotherhood mortal enemies with the [[Casterwill family]] and sworn on revenge. {{Source|Chasing Void}} 
Throughout the generations, the Blood Spiral remained hidden, hunting down and eliminating whole branches of the Casterwill family. {{Source|Chasing Void}} One of their young hunters, the pyromaniac [[Kiel]], succeeded in setting the [[Paris Casterwill house]] aflame, killing the parents of [[Sophie Casterwill]] and separating her from her big brother, [[Lucas Casterwill|Lucas]]. {{Source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

At some point in time, [[Rassimov]] began working for [[the Organization]], in order to cripple them from the inside. He rose through their ranks to become one of [[the Professor]]'s most senior operatives before setting up his downfall to the Huntik team by giving the [[Amulet]] of [[Archwarder]] to [[Dante Vale]]. {{Source|The Divine Comedy}} With this Titan, the [[Huntik Foundation]] was able to weaken the [[Legendary Titan]] of Immortality, [[Overlos]], defeat [[the Professor]] and send his Legendary Titans back to the [[Spirit World]], successfully removing the Professor as a threat to the Blood Spiral's goals. {{source|The Mission}}

After the fall of [[the Professor]], the Blood Spiral Brotherhood emerged from the shadows of history and revealed themselves to both the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[the Organization]] alike at [[Klaus' bookshop]]. There they recovered the Amulet of the evil [[Void]] in order to resurrect the rest of the [[Nullifiers]] and left the destruction in their wake. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}
